A||N||3||beachbomb||Timing gear finally complete(YEA!!!)||||10||
Z||000000||beachbomb||08-08-2001||03:58 PM||||Hey all, well after three weeks and alot of work i finally replaced my stripped out timing gear on my Indy!! Here's how i did it,<BR>i pulled the engine out(firgured it would be easier this way since i had just pulled another engine 2 weeks earlier!!), once it was out and mounted on an engine stand, i pulled out the cam and replaced the gear, since the engine was out i also replaced the oil pump, and water pump!! And re-did most of the seals. Re-installed the engine and when i went to start it..................................................it started right up!!!(THANK GOODNESS!!!) i had an exhaust leak which i found to be the exhaust flange gasket(i put it in a little sideways), fixed that the next day, i also have a small oil leak, looks like it coming from that stupid oil pan engineering flaw!!! So when i get more time i'll hjave to pull the pan again and re-do the seal. The car runs alot smoother now! This is the first time i have ever gone inside an engine!!! i am so proud that i actually did something like this. When the engine i was i thoroughly inspected the inside of the engine, i found no oil build-up or sludge anywhere, looked like a new engine. This actually surprised me, because with 180,000 miles, i thought i would see some of that. I'm just glad i have my Indy back <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Special thanks goes out to Dale Houston for all the e-mail help he provided!!!! If you have any questions about the timing gear changeout, please email me.....later, i have to go cruise for a while...Jim (2 '84 Indys)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigzach_21.JPG"> ||||reg||10
Z||000001||Raydar||08-08-2001||04:27 PM||||Cool!||||reg||14
Z||000002||starfighter007@msn.com||08-08-2001||07:51 PM||||I am impressed.Bravo to you bummer about that oil leak though,I hate when that happens.But all in all sounds like you did a good job.||||reg||1
Z||000003||beachbomb||08-08-2001||09:05 PM||||Thanks all, yea the oil leaks ticks me off, i used alot of RTV on the seals, it appears to be coming from the oil pan on the transmission side where there are no screws for the oil pan, just RTV(where i put alot of it!! Oh well, Jim||||reg||6
